{"ranking": ["M10", "M2", "M4"], "fault": "M10 (the diode-connected NMOS that sets the cascode gate node nc) has L=0.5 um, which doubles its W/L relative to the L=1 used by the other bias devices. This lowers its Vgs and pulls nc too low, so M2 cannot hold s1 high enough to keep M1 in saturation. That explains the low gain (14 dB), the reduced GBW, and the output being pulled low (0.17 V). The likely correction is restoring M10 to L=1."}
